    "done_when": "reckon crew dispatch gains an --accept-directory-claim flag. With a live run claiming tests/test_x.py, a dry-run declaring the directory tests as a write path returns a warning that names the overlapping claim and the owning run, lists the files the brief names as the exact alternative, and does not proceed. The same dry-run with --accept-directory-claim proceeds and records that the flag was given. A declared file path that overlaps nothing, and a directory overlapping no live claim, dispatch as before with no warning. tests/test_directory_claim_asks_first.py covers those four cases through the dispatch entry point, using a live run whose launcher pid is alive. Base and head arms over every tests/ file whose AST imports reckon.crew.dispatch run with -n 4 and a separate --basetemp under /tmp each, both logs end with an EXIT= line, the file list is in both logs, and the head adds no failing test id. Before status complete, delete every directory you created under /tmp, print what you delete, and list it in artifacts.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
